README.md-444-| `csk install [target]` | Apply `Skillfile.json` using current git refs. Missing `git` URL sources are cloned into `skills_root`; existing local repositories are not fetched. No target means current project; `target` may be an alias, `.`, or a project path. |
README.md-445-| `csk install --audit [strict]` | Run the audit gate for this install only. Without `strict`, audit is advisory and does not change config. |
README.md-446-| `csk install --all` | Install every project explicitly registered in global config. |
README.md-447-| `csk update` | Fetch all git repositories under `skills_root`. Does not modify projects. |
README.md:448:| `csk upgrade [target]` | Fetch only the selected project's direct and transitive skill repositories, then install. `--dry-run` does not update cached repositories or persist files. |
README.md-449-| `csk upgrade --all` | Fetch the union of dependency closures once, then install every registered project. |
README.md-450-| `csk status [target]` | Show manifest vs installed state, including active dev substitutions. `--check` exits non-zero unless everything is up-to-date; `--json` prints machine-readable output. |
README.md-451-| `csk status --all` | Show status for every registered project. |
README.md-452-| `csk add <name> --tag/--branch/--revision ...` | Add or replace a skill declaration in the project Skillfile; apply with `csk install`. |
README.md-453-| `csk remove <name>` | Remove a skill declaration from the project Skillfile; the next install cleans generated files. |
README.md:454:| `csk gc` | Remove unreferenced runtime entries, snapshot cache entries, and dead consumer registry entries. |
README.md-455-| `csk audit [target]` | Run skill security audit for the current project, an alias, `.`, or a project path. Supports `--all`, `--global`, and `--json`. |
README.md-456-| `csk skill check <dir>` | Validate one skill directory without requiring global config or project setup. |
README.md-457-| `csk list [--paths]` | List configured projects and declared skills. |
README.md-458-| `csk project add <alias> <path>` | Register a project for `--all` and create a manifest if missing. |
README.md-459-| `csk project resolve [target]` | Show resolved project alias, checkout alias, Skillfile, and install paths. |
README.md-460-| `csk global init` | Create the user-wide global `Skillfile.json`, global skill context, bin, and env files. |
README.md-461-| `csk global add <name> --tag/--branch/--revision ...` | Add or replace a global skill declaration. |
README.md-462-| `csk global remove <name>` | Remove a global declaration; the next global install cleans generated files. |
README.md-463-| `csk global install` | Install all globally declared skills without fetching. |
README.md-464-| `csk global update` | Fetch source repositories for globally declared skills. |
README.md-465-| `csk global upgrade` | Run global update, then global install. `--dry-run` skips the update and performs a non-persistent install plan. |
README.md-466-| `csk global status` | Show global manifest vs installed state. |
README.md-467-| `csk global list` | List global skill declarations. |
README.md-468-| `csk config show` | Print resolved config path and contents. |
README.md:469:| `csk shell-init [auto\|zsh\|bash\|powershell]` | Optionally print shell hook code for human-facing global and project-local auto-`PATH` activation. The default `auto` detects the current environment; `--install` atomically caches it and prints the profile source command; `--no-global` limits activation to project checkouts. Agent execution does not require this hook. |
README.md-470-| `csk --version` | Print version and exit. |
