docs/v0.11-design.md-121-  one of those keys.
docs/v0.11-design.md-122-- The snapshot defends freshness. A client stores the highest snapshot version
docs/v0.11-design.md-123-  it has seen per registry and refuses a snapshot whose version moved backward,
docs/v0.11-design.md-124-  which detects rollback. A snapshot older than a configured maximum age is
docs/v0.11-design.md-125-  stale, and the client treats lookups against it as unavailable.
docs/v0.11-design.md-126-- Equal-version snapshots must retain the same head, Merkle root, and log size.
docs/v0.11-design.md-127-  The high-water state is keyed by canonical registry URL and survives signing
docs/v0.11-design.md-128-  key rotation. It lives in protected durable state outside the disposable
docs/v0.11-design.md:129:  response cache. Existing corruption and persistence failure are fail-closed.
docs/v0.11-design.md-130-- The transparency log makes issuance auditable. Every record enters an
docs/v0.11-design.md-131-  append-only, hash-chained log, so an auditor can verify that the set of
docs/v0.11-design.md-132-  records a registry serves matches the set it has ever logged.
docs/v0.11-design.md-133-
docs/v0.11-design.md-134-This is a reduced profile of The Update Framework: pinned roots plus a signed
docs/v0.11-design.md-135-snapshot and timestamp, without delegated roles. A full delegation hierarchy is
docs/v0.11-design.md-136-future work (section 14).
docs/v0.11-design.md-137-
