docs/v0.11-design.md-186-## 8. Resolution at install time
docs/v0.11-design.md-187-
docs/v0.11-design.md-188-The audit gate gains a registry step, run against the same content snapshot the
docs/v0.11-design.md-189-install pipeline already produced.
docs/v0.11-design.md-190-
docs/v0.11-design.md-191-1. Compute the content hash of the skill snapshot, which the pipeline already
docs/v0.11-design.md-192-   does.
docs/v0.11-design.md-193-2. Refresh each trusted registry's snapshot, subject to the freshness rules. A
docs/v0.11-design.md:194:   registry that cannot be reached uses the last cached snapshot within the
docs/v0.11-design.md-195-   offline grace window, with a warning.
docs/v0.11-design.md-196-3. Look up the artifact by `source_identity` and `commit`, and by
docs/v0.11-design.md-197-   `content_sha256`, in each trusted registry. Verify every returned record
docs/v0.11-design.md-198-   against the registry's pinned keys.
docs/v0.11-design.md-199-4. Apply the federation rule to reach a status, then apply policy.
docs/v0.11-design.md-200-5. Record the authorizing attestation in the install marker: the registry name,
docs/v0.11-design.md-201-   the record, and the verifying key id.
docs/v0.11-design.md-202-
--
docs/v0.11-design.md-251-## 12. Failure catalog
docs/v0.11-design.md-252-
docs/v0.11-design.md-253-Resolution surfaces a specific outcome when:
docs/v0.11-design.md-254-
docs/v0.11-design.md-255-- a record signature does not verify against any pinned key for its registry:
docs/v0.11-design.md-256-  the record is ignored and a warning is emitted;
docs/v0.11-design.md-257-- a snapshot version moved backward, or a snapshot is older than the maximum
docs/v0.11-design.md-258-  age: the registry is treated as unavailable;
docs/v0.11-design.md:259:- a trusted registry cannot be reached and no cached snapshot is within the
docs/v0.11-design.md-260-  grace window: the registry is unavailable, and strict policy fails the
docs/v0.11-design.md-261-  install;
docs/v0.11-design.md-262-- the artifact is unknown to every trusted registry: policy decides;
docs/v0.11-design.md-263-- any trusted registry returns `revoked`: the install is denied.
docs/v0.11-design.md-264-
docs/v0.11-design.md-265-## 13. Compatibility
docs/v0.11-design.md-266-
docs/v0.11-design.md-267-- Existing installs are unaffected. With no `audit_registries` configured and
--
docs/v0.11-design.md-295-  16 MiB;
docs/v0.11-design.md-296-- GET retries are limited to network errors, `429`, and `503`; publication
docs/v0.11-design.md-297-  retries require the identical record bytes and deterministic
docs/v0.11-design.md-298-  `Idempotency-Key`; every loop has three total attempts and a finite total
docs/v0.11-design.md-299-  deadline;
docs/v0.11-design.md-300-- redirects are rejected, so queries do not change and bearer tokens do not
docs/v0.11-design.md-301-  move to another endpoint;
docs/v0.11-design.md-302-- rollback state is stored under the machine `state/registry` directory,
docs/v0.11-design.md:303:  migrated from the legacy response-cache location, written atomically before
docs/v0.11-design.md-304-  acceptance, and included in protected machine backups.
docs/v0.11-design.md-305-
docs/v0.11-design.md-306-These behaviors are executed from the authoritative `registry-client.json`
docs/v0.11-design.md-307-vectors on Linux, macOS, and Windows.
