docs/mvp-design.md:804:who want automatic bare project commands may opt into a one-time cached hook.
docs/mvp-design.md-805-`csk shell-init --install` auto-detects zsh/bash from `SHELL`, Git Bash before
docs/mvp-design.md-806-the Windows fallback, and PowerShell on Windows. An explicit shell argument
docs/mvp-design.md-807-remains available.
docs/mvp-design.md-808-
docs/mvp-design.md-809-`csk shell-init zsh` and `csk shell-init bash` print a hook that:
docs/mvp-design.md-810-
docs/mvp-design.md-811-- runs on prompt or directory change;
docs/mvp-design.md-812-- searches upward for `.agents/env.sh`;
--
docs/mvp-design.md-817-`.agents/env.ps1`.
docs/mvp-design.md-818-
docs/mvp-design.md-819-Since v0.6.0, `csk shell-init` also activates the user-wide global scope from
docs/mvp-design.md-820-`~/.cocoaskills/global/env.sh` or `env.ps1` before project-local activation.
docs/mvp-design.md-821-This makes global commands available outside project checkouts while preserving
docs/mvp-design.md-822-project-local shadowing inside managed projects.
docs/mvp-design.md-823-
docs/mvp-design.md-824-`csk bootstrap` states that no shell profile changes are required and may point
docs/mvp-design.md:825:to the optional cached hook for human convenience. `csk install` reports an
docs/mvp-design.md-826-off-`PATH` project bin as informational: agent skills use it directly.
docs/mvp-design.md-827-Project and global runtime shims prepend their own bin directory, the Python
docs/mvp-design.md-828-environment that installed them, and the resolved directories of declared
docs/mvp-design.md-829-system dependencies before preserving the inherited `PATH`. Nested skill
docs/mvp-design.md-830-commands therefore work from zsh, bash, PowerShell, Git Bash, CI, and agent
docs/mvp-design.md-831-processes without profile activation.
