docs/v0.9-design.md-19-- A workflow is a skill that declares dependencies and exports no commands. A consumer installs a workflow with a single `Skillfile.json` entry.
docs/v0.9-design.md-20-
docs/v0.9-design.md-21-## 2. Motivating cases
docs/v0.9-design.md-22-
docs/v0.9-design.md-23-Two recurring cases drive the design.
docs/v0.9-design.md-24-
docs/v0.9-design.md-25-An orchestrator skill runs a multi-step process. Its SKILL.md delegates whole steps to provider skills such as an issue tracker, a monitoring client, and a review tool: the agent reads their instructions and runs their commands. The orchestrator publishes that composition once; a consumer installs the workflow with one project entry.
docs/v0.9-design.md-26-
docs/v0.9-design.md:27:A library-style skill builds on a command that another skill exports. The consumer's scripts call the provider executable, the binary is available on `PATH`, and the usage is documented in the consumer's own SKILL.md. The requirement is reproducible: csk fetches the provider and installs the command.
docs/v0.9-design.md-28-
docs/v0.9-design.md-29-The first case activates entire skills. The second activates a single command. The mode field covers both.
docs/v0.9-design.md-30-
docs/v0.9-design.md-31-## 3. Requirement manifest
docs/v0.9-design.md-32-
docs/v0.9-design.md-33-Requirements live in `csk-skill.json` schema v4 under `dependencies.skills`.
