docs/v0.8-design.md-107-- If redaction changes any file, the request has `redacted=true`.
docs/v0.8-design.md-108-- Backend output must be parsed into `Finding`; malformed output is a backend
docs/v0.8-design.md-109-  failure, not a finding.
docs/v0.8-design.md-110-- Backends may add findings but must not remove static findings.
docs/v0.8-design.md-111-- Backend findings must set `verifiable=true` only when the finding is anchored
docs/v0.8-design.md-112-  to a concrete file/span or another deterministic piece of evidence. Findings
docs/v0.8-design.md-113-  that are useful but not checkable must set `verifiable=false`.
docs/v0.8-design.md-114-- The install gate considers static findings and verifiable backend findings
docs/v0.8-design.md:115:  only. Unverifiable backend findings are kept in reports and cache as advisory
docs/v0.8-design.md-116-  facts, but a hallucinated high-severity finding must not block install.
docs/v0.8-design.md-117-- Static detector findings are deterministic and gate-eligible.
docs/v0.8-design.md-118-- Backends must not return policy decisions.
docs/v0.8-design.md-119-
docs/v0.8-design.md-120-Backend canary:
docs/v0.8-design.md-121-
docs/v0.8-design.md-122-- `run_canary()` sends a built-in malicious fixture through the backend before
docs/v0.8-design.md-123-  the backend is trusted for real skills.
--
docs/v0.8-design.md-200-- If `cloud=false`, `oss=true` and `local_provider` are required. A Codex
docs/v0.8-design.md-201-  backend cannot be treated as local unless the config names the local provider.
docs/v0.8-design.md-202-- If `cloud=true`, `oss` and `local_provider` are rejected.
docs/v0.8-design.md-203-
docs/v0.8-design.md-204-Cloud rules:
docs/v0.8-design.md-205-
docs/v0.8-design.md-206-- If selected backend config has `cloud=true`, `audit.allow_cloud` must be true.
docs/v0.8-design.md-207-- If selected backend config has `cloud=false`, file contents are not redacted
docs/v0.8-design.md:208:  for egress, but evidence redaction still applies before cache/output.
docs/v0.8-design.md-209-- If source classification is not `public` and backend is cloud, fail closed
docs/v0.8-design.md-210-  unless the backend config explicitly sets `allow_internal_sources: true`.
docs/v0.8-design.md-211-  This field is not accepted in v0.8. It is reserved for a later policy review.
