docs/audit-design.md-429-- Per-skill grants: a legitimate skill that must read `~/.aws` (a cloud skill) or
docs/audit-design.md-430-  run git declares it in `capabilities`; a human reviews and pins the grant. A
docs/audit-design.md-431-  grant is `(skill, capability, content_sha256, who, when, reason)`.
docs/audit-design.md-432-- Legacy pin: `csk audit --allow <hash> --reason "..."` clears only the
docs/audit-design.md-433-  schema v1/v2 capability-declaration requirement and records the decision with
docs/audit-design.md-434-  provenance. It does not override strict finding-level blocks.
docs/audit-design.md-435-- Revocation: a blocklist of `(source | content_hash)` blocks installs even when
docs/audit-design.md-436-  an old pass verdict exists.
docs/audit-design.md:437:- Shared verdict cache: keyed by `(content_sha256, backend, model,
docs/audit-design.md-438-  prompt_version, ruleset_version)` in `~/.cocoaskills/audit/`. Auditing
docs/audit-design.md-439-  skill-X@commit once serves every project that installs it.
